=== llvm-ar-18 ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
OVERVIEW: LLVM Archiver


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  llvm-ar-18 [options] [-]<operation>[modifiers] [relpos] [count] <archive>
      [files]
  llvm-ar-18 -M [<mri-script]


POSITIONALS (4) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  relpos
  count
  archive
  files


FLAGS (10) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    --format          archive format to create
                        values:
                          default     default
                          gnu         gnu
                          darwin      darwin
                          bsd         bsd
                          bigarchive  big archive (AIX OS)
    --plugin <string> ignored for compatibility
-h, --help            display this help and exit
    --output          the directory to extract archive members to
    --rsp-quoting     quoting style for response files
                        values:
                          posix    posix
                          windows  windows
    --thin            create a thin archive
    --version         print the version and exit
-X {32|64|32_64|any}  object mode (only for AIX OS)
@<file>               read options from <file>
-M [<mri-script]


MODIFIERS (19) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Modifiers
a     put [files] after [relpos]
b     put [files] before [relpos] (same as [i])
c     do not warn if archive had to be created
D     use zero for timestamps and uids/gids (default)
h     display this help and exit
i     put [files] before [relpos] (same as [b])
l     ignored for compatibility
L     add archive's contents
N     use instance [count] of name
o     preserve original dates
O     display member offsets
P     use full names when matching (implied for thin archives)
s     create an archive index (cf. ranlib)
S     do not build a symbol table
T     deprecated, use --thin instead
u     update only [files] newer than archive contents
U     use actual timestamps and uids/gids
v     be verbose about actions taken
V     display the version and exit

=== llvm-ar-18 d ===
delete [files] from the archive

=== llvm-ar-18 m ===
move [files] in the archive

=== llvm-ar-18 p ===
print contents of [files] found in the archive

=== llvm-ar-18 q ===
quick append [files] to the archive

=== llvm-ar-18 r ===
replace or insert [files] into the archive

=== llvm-ar-18 s ===
act as ranlib

=== llvm-ar-18 t ===
display list of files in archive

=== llvm-ar-18 x ===
extract [files] from the archive
